-- title:
--   Value of `Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` on fractions s/r^k
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring equipped with a grading $\mathcal A : \mathbb N \to \sigma$ by additive subgroups making it a graded ring, let $X$ be a scheme, and let $g : A \to \Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X)$ be a ring homomorphism whose image of the irrelevant ideal generates the unit ideal, i.e. the ideal of $\Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X)$ generated by $g$ of `HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒜` is $\top$; these data determine the morphism $\theta_g =$ `Proj.fromOfGlobalSections 𝒜 g hg` from $X$ to $\operatorname{Proj}\mathcal A$. Let $n$ be a positive natural number, $r \in \mathcal A_n$, $k$ a natural number and $s \in \mathcal A_{k\cdot n}$. Since $\theta_g^{-1}(D_+(r)) = X_{g(r)}$, one has the induced map on sections $\Gamma(D_+(r), \mathcal O_{\operatorname{Proj}\mathcal A}) \to \Gamma(X_{g(r)}, \mathcal O_X)$ given by `appLE` along this inclusion of opens. The assertion is that the image under this map of the section `Proj.awayToSection 𝒜 r` attached to the degree-zero homogeneous localisation element $s/r^k \in (A_r)_0$, multiplied by the $k$-th power of the restriction of $g(r)$ to $X_{g(r)}$, equals the restriction of $g(s)$ to $X_{g(r)}$.
--
--   This records the comorphism of the canonical morphism $X \to \operatorname{Proj} \mathcal A$ attached to a ring homomorphism from a graded ring into the global sections of $X$, evaluated on the standard generators $s/r^k$ of the sections over a basic open $D_+(r)$: it is the fraction $g(s)/g(r)^k$. It is used in the construction of the canonical morphism to $\operatorname{Proj}$ for a graded algebra of sections, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.GradedOAlgebra.IsSectionRing.exists_isCanonicalToProj`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.GradedOAlgebra.IsSectionRing.exists_isCanonicalToProj).
